<h2 local-id=3D"cd5e9199-c9c7-4d9e-9bd1-6fcd689790db" id=3D"TSD-ATSDataPart=
itioning-Overview">Overview</h2>
<p local-id=3D"0f61ddf9-7729-468b-b654-98875ba39650">This is the technical =
solution document for Data partitioning in fast growing tables in Transacti=
on Database.</p>
<h3 local-id=3D"d4be401c-97ea-4b26-a7d1-c59adf211f50" id=3D"TSD-ATSDataPart=
itioning-EPIC:">EPIC:</h3>
<p local-id=3D"d402a61f-e6a3-4c9a-8325-07f59fe9cd5c"><br><a class=3D"extern=
al-link" data-card-appearance=3D"inline" href=3D"https://zeta-axon.atlassia=
n.net/browse/ACO-5033" local-id=3D"609bf04d-a2c7-4da2-8de3-e67149374847" re=
l=3D"nofollow">https://zeta-axon.atlassian.net/browse/ACO-5033</a></p>
<h3 local-id=3D"4ed9fe30-1e9c-435d-b40b-fed9f0b7331f" id=3D"TSD-ATSDataPart=
itioning-ProblemStatement">Problem Statement</h3>
<p local-id=3D"5ef44d47-54c7-4604-9fc9-5223ada6b4c4">The transaction data i=
n the PostgreSQL database has grown to approximately 1TB, leading to perfor=
mance degradation in queries and maintenance tasks. The current single-tabl=
e structure results in slower query performance, and makes data management =
(such as purging old data) cumbersome. A scalable solution is required to o=
ptimize query performance and efficiently manage data volume.</p>
<h3 local-id=3D"9bda4166-3c4d-4b05-aff2-984932c66d42" id=3D"TSD-ATSDataPart=
itioning-Solution">Solution</h3>
<ul local-id=3D"7d1c8859-39b6-4772-a535-a5721fee29c5">
<li local-id=3D"7c51472f-2e6e-429a-a4b1-08f329706db0">
<p local-id=3D"021a195b-e39f-4b90-aa7c-916580bf2064">To resolve above issue=
s we are considering Data partitioning.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"51dc9211-6abd-45ac-bcb3-d1b5b5195e01">
<p local-id=3D"4d3ddcbf-d19e-4459-a3a7-091d03ada5e3">What is the impact of =
change - Proposed change will help in managing the data more efficiently as=
 old partitions can be easily archived and storage costs can be kept in con=
trol</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"fe2826af-9d63-4393-9cf7-8e762732c16b">
<p local-id=3D"a464c198-4233-473e-9494-492b76f81667">From Axon Transaction =
Service we need to return 30 days data atleast, in newly created partition =
tables data won=E2=80=99t present and copying old data to partition tables =
is very challenging as we have huge data copying takes a lot of time and it=
 impacts database heavily which may cause services to go down as well. So i=
norder to prevent this we are going with following approach</p>
<ul local-id=3D"7c3e2819-41bb-4721-8480-6093022c16b6">
<li local-id=3D"04f2754e-a917-4463-b34a-83c0e2dc7fd1">
<p local-id=3D"4bf8c9b6-de12-46a2-be81-d67fcd23ec1c">Create a New Partition=
 tables in new database (Suggested by DB team)</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"70eb7724-2164-4b8c-b0b0-2159075e5a50">
<p local-id=3D"4a0fae35-e36c-460a-8179-e02b7913c70b">Now Sync this database=
 with running database for 2 months as a buffer we added extra 30 days</p><=
/li>
<li local-id=3D"ff61c5d1-550b-43c9-80b5-06fc6a5d44f4">
<p local-id=3D"1b26ead9-1152-4704-af25-1c2265cc848a">At the cut off date af=
ter 2months, with very small downtime we change our database to Partition d=
atabase.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"d583b368-f877-4385-af38-051795c662b5">
<p local-id=3D"d9070d81-e200-4e27-b34b-cbd452639dd2">With this approach dow=
ntime is few minutes only.</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ul>
<h2 local-id=3D"ae05e6ad-37b3-4149-808e-aaed141d7aba" id=3D"TSD-ATSDataPart=
itioning-TechSolution">Tech Solution</h2>
<h3 local-id=3D"69c02219-00e0-41d0-aa2a-0ccd8c3de472" id=3D"TSD-ATSDataPart=
itioning-PartitionTableDesign">Partition Table Design</h3>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"56489be0-cc79-4e69-ba6e-ae224b64d159">
<li local-id=3D"4ecfcb55-88ac-43d2-a23e-77745e45082b">
<p local-id=3D"ed01ca3e-17a4-4718-9348-5a645a0090d6"><strong><span class=3D=
"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"7e79cea7-62ad-4407-b954-a27e0604908d">P=
arent Table </span>:</strong> The parent table acts as a template and does =
not store any data directly. It defines the common structure and primary ke=
y.</p></li>
</ol>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: java; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">Sample =
Partition table
CREATE TABLE transaction_child (
    id BIGINT NOT NULL,
    ---, --&gt; transaction_child columns
    created_at TIMESTAMP NOT NULL
    PRIMARY KEY (id,created_at)
) PARTITION BY RANGE (created_at);</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p local-id=3D"e22b8e81-d128-4f61-8dda-1f27dd5e0603"></p>
<ol start=3D"2" local-id=3D"e85dc001-12d8-49c0-9554-27f409cc86a5">
<li local-id=3D"be748357-b588-4afd-b1c8-7095acb80b0f">
<p local-id=3D"425f660d-b0b7-486a-9436-f1b099745a0e"><strong>Monthly Partit=
ions:</strong> Monthly partitions will be created dynamically based on the =
<code>created_at</code> field using the <code>pg_partman</code> extension t=
o automate partition management.</p></li>
</ol>
<p local-id=3D"c9f68f63-4641-46c6-b0af-6f73cb6f22e3">Example:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: java; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">Sample

SELECT partman.create_parent(
    p_parent_table :=3D '&lt;schema_name&gt;.transaction_child',
    p_control :=3D 'created_at',
    p_type :=3D 'native',
    p_interval :=3D 'monthly'
);</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p local-id=3D"be6877e3-1c11-475d-b9ee-e1ea65f8024b"></p>
<ol start=3D"3" local-id=3D"5967ba40-8ca4-49a9-bfd4-39d2e745f0c7">
<li local-id=3D"c5c9c22d-e97a-4828-a886-9f162ea083e4">
<p local-id=3D"c7cb23c9-cdaa-4d9b-91e1-18858fe5c769"><strong>Default Partit=
ion:</strong> A default partition will capture data that does not fall into=
 any specific range.</p></li>
</ol>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: java; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">Sample
CREATE TABLE transaction_child_default
PARTITION OF transaction_child DEFAULT;</pre>
</div>
</div>
<ol start=3D"4" local-id=3D"082aa9d0-6b31-4c99-b45f-b15952115b0d">
<li local-id=3D"f557d60b-932c-4fff-9d5c-7937eb3b9baf">
<p local-id=3D"62e9d0d0-9a78-49c5-a4e5-ba672f0f7a00"><strong>Sequence for I=
D:</strong> A single sequence will be used for the <code>id</code> column a=
cross all partitions for each table</p></li>
</ol>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: java; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">CREATE =
SEQUENCE IF NOT EXISTS transaction_child_id_seq AS BIGINT;

ALTER TABLE transaction_child ALTER COLUMN id SET DEFAULT nextval('transact=
ion_child_id_seq');</pre>
</div>
</div>
<ol start=3D"5" local-id=3D"9320198a-92c8-4e98-9bcb-68f7fcf17a71">
<li local-id=3D"6ac82f34-2d5d-4e74-946d-28ddd9405068">
<p local-id=3D"f65f05a1-f717-4d76-ad6f-4e0eebfdf4b6"><strong>Detaching Olde=
r Partitions: </strong>Partitions older than two months will be detached an=
d archived or dropped, this operation is also done using pg_partman extensi=
on in automated way.</p></li>
</ol>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: java; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">ALTER T=
ABLE partman.part_config
    SET p_premake :=3D 2,  -- Number of partitions to pre-create (e.g., cur=
rent + previous month)
    p_retention :=3D '2 months', -- Retain only the current and previous mo=
nth's partitions
    p_retention_keep_table :=3D true; -- Automatically detach older partiti=
ons instead of dropping them</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p local-id=3D"a0623fe2-73b3-4d53-bcdc-75886c2342ba">5. <strong>Matching Qu=
ery Updates </strong>: In existing queries we pass a field created_at as ad=
ditional query param to improve query performance by checking specific part=
ition only. In Axon as we release transaction for 7 days old transactions s=
o will add query param value so as to get All matching transactions created=
 in last 7 days only.</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: java; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">Sample =
Query Update

SELECT * FROM transaction_view WHERE tenant_id =3D $1 AND is_deleted =3D $2=
=20
AND payment_account_id =3D $3  AND processing_network_type =3D $4 =20
AND settlement_date =3D $5  AND system_trace_audit_number =3D $6=20
AND banknet_reference =3D $7
AND created_at &gt;=3D (Date value in dd-mm-yyy - 7 days)</pre>
</div>
</div>
<h3 local-id=3D"e5f8bec8-4f35-470f-8390-a19f3573eaa7" id=3D"TSD-ATSDataPart=
itioning-Overview.1">Overview</h3>
<p local-id=3D"08c85af3-ed78-495a-b154-a2ec3b7c3421">To address the challen=
ges of handling large transaction data, partitioning the table by month bas=
ed on the <code>created_at</code> timestamp is proposed.</p>
<p local-id=3D"0c0e2881-d329-445b-bf44-c806e619be68">This approach will:</p=
>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"54bc8d24-beea-4394-b121-bf4d180a998c">
<li local-id=3D"8213bda5-638d-44be-927d-8006d404b4ae">
<p local-id=3D"6b78e254-618f-48cc-a9f2-228bfb6d3c07">Improve query performa=
nce by targeting specific partitions.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"315af263-6b98-44c1-89d5-5a0bc958485e">
<p local-id=3D"d51d4ceb-0544-48bc-9ebf-85bea53eed4d">Simplify data manageme=
nt by detaching older partitions.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"d7d4656a-9927-4c3d-931c-ef4beee038ae">
<p local-id=3D"613a1b57-cf93-4052-961d-35697e8c8fc2">Maintain compatibility=
 with the current application by using the same table and column structure.=
</p></li>
</ol>
<p local-id=3D"5b66abe2-861a-4182-99bc-3249f818fc9e">The partitioning will:=
</p>
<ul local-id=3D"aa9fa8ad-259e-4469-a401-e68bc8fc18ac">
<li local-id=3D"4c79d3d0-c482-408c-88a7-666805b2d0d8">
<p local-id=3D"80717f4c-8360-411a-9315-a7f6eb2202db">Use monthly partitions=
.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"422076bc-c189-4893-8848-f645bd8a0af7">
<p local-id=3D"f3bffbd2-b07f-4dd5-bfe8-0a0ca5d057ae">Include a default part=
ition for edge-case data.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"498506d7-4c15-4e88-9712-2b0f7b0b245e">
<p local-id=3D"5ce8cf28-c688-4374-944a-5efba67172b9">Retain the <code>id</c=
ode> column as a primary key with a common sequence across all partitions t=
o avoid duplicate IDs.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"be4c4e50-680a-4ff2-9431-879578654998">
<p local-id=3D"fb8ed525-bdb8-4f6c-b202-86a9f2748354">Mirror the indexes of =
the current table in all partitions for efficient query performance.</p></l=
i>
</ul>
